  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\sqrt{5-x}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=\\sqrt{5-x}.$ Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14253135/assets/f22f3680e9637e1630a01fe8b89c4b1f8252822908c1c2d162c88be0610c65c8.png)\n\nWe see that the function is not defined for $x>5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$",
